    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a favorable slate today, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Junior Caminero** (81.92). **Yordan Alvarez** is the clear priority, benefitting from a premium matchup against Shane Bieber, whose 5.48 xERA suggests he is vulnerable to elite sluggers; his xwOBA of 0.477 provides the highest ceiling in our lineup. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** capitalizes on an advantageous park factor and a soft matchup against Michael Lorenzen. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** remains an essential start (75.84) not just for his expected production, but for his specific utility in our 5x5 build: facing a slower-to-the-plate Bubba Chandler, **Christian Yelich** earns a fractional boost for his stolen base potential, a critical category for us to maintain our edge.\n\nWhile the lineup is largely locked, the decision to bench **Nelson Velazquez** (38.73) was the most difficult. He fell just short of the 40-point \"marginal\" threshold, primarily due to an unfavorable matchup against Cam Schlittler; Schlittler\u2019s 2.85 xERA suppresses the offensive environment, ultimately dragging **Nelson Velazquez** into the below-floor category and forcing us to prioritize the higher-upside profiles of **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. We remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players; should official lineups shift our assumed batting order, specifically for **Gary Sanchez** or **Kazuma Okamoto**, the efficiency scores may fluctuate. We are closely monitoring the environment for the games involving **Lars Nootbaar**, as he faces the stiffest test of the day against Schlittler; his projection is heavily reliant on the top-of-the-order designation, and any drop in his lineup position could necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of his status.",
